    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on some preliminary risk assessments for our new urban development fund. We're looking at some sectors in the downtown/eastside corridor that have seen a lot of rapid demographic shifts and new immigrant communities moving in over the last 24 months. From a long-term actuarial standpoint, what kind of social or economic volatility indicators should we be tracking to gauge the stability of these specific types of neighborhoods for 10-year+ investments?",
